# Web3Forms access key for the service request form.
#
# THIS KEY IS THE DESTINATION. Web3Forms binds the recipient inbox to the key
# itself — there is no "to" field in the payload and no way to redirect a
# submission from the code. To change where requests land you must issue a NEW
# key against the new inbox and replace the value below. Editing anything in
# src/ will not move a single email.
#
# Current intended destination: info@mail.aqmasters.com
#
# The form has two delivery paths and chooses automatically:
#
#   key set        → Web3Forms. Relays to the inbox the key was issued for.
#   no key, localhost / npm run dev
#                  → Preview. The form validates fully, delivers nothing, and
#                    says so plainly on the confirmation screen. It never
#                    reports a success that did not happen.
#   no key, in production
#                  → Unconfigured. NO form is rendered at all; a panel points
#                    at the phone number and email instead. This is deliberate:
#                    taking details we cannot deliver is worse than no form.
#
# (There was a third path, Netlify Forms. It is gone — the site is on Vercel,
# which has no equivalent.)
#
# Every build prints which path it produced. See GOING-LIVE.md section 2.
#
# Get a key free at https://web3forms.com — enter the destination inbox and the
# key is emailed to it. It is safe to expose in client-side code. It must be
# present at BUILD time (Vite inlines it), so set it in Vercel's environment
# variables too and redeploy — changing it locally alone does nothing to prod.
VITE_WEB3FORMS_KEY=
